(AND (IMPLIES (AND (NOT (ENDP RULES))
                   (NOT (AND (NOT (EQ (RULE-MATCH (CAR RULES) X) :FAIL))
                             (EQUAL (INSTANTIATE (CADDR (CAR RULES))
                                                 (RULE-MATCH (CAR RULES) X))
                                    U)))
                   (:P RULE (CDR RULES) U X))
              (:P RULE RULES U X))
     (IMPLIES (AND (NOT (ENDP RULES))
                   (AND (NOT (EQ (RULE-MATCH (CAR RULES) X) :FAIL))
                        (EQUAL (INSTANTIATE (CADDR (CAR RULES))
                                            (RULE-MATCH (CAR RULES) X))
                               U)))
              (:P RULE RULES U X))
     (IMPLIES (ENDP RULES)
              (:P RULE RULES U X))).
This induction is justified by the same argument used to admit 
ROOT-STEP-RULES.  When applied to the goal at hand the above induction
scheme produces three nontautological subgoals.
